# Custom DRC rules — HV Pi Hat (5 kV DEA driver, conformal-coated)
# Auto-loaded by KiCad/pcbnew because this file is named "<project>.kicad_dru".
#
# HV nets live in netclass HV_5kV (rail + per-channel outputs + discharge nodes).
#
# REVISED 2026-06-08 (user/EE-approved, see docs/AUTONOMOUS_BUILD_LOG.md): at 85x56 the
# 2-channel active-discharge HV routes only at ~2 mm spacing. The user (EE) selected the
# CONFORMAL-COATED + FR4-ENCASED design: HV runs primarily on the INNER copper layers
# (In1/In2), encased in FR4 (~20 kV/mm bulk strength -> safe at 2 mm for 5 kV), with the
# outer-layer HV protected by conformal coating. Under IEC 60664 a coated/sealed surface
# (effective pollution degree 1) drops the 5 kV creepage requirement to ~2 mm, matching the
# 2 mm air clearance (creepage >= air, so 2 mm is the binding figure). => CREEPAGE held at
# 2 mm. JLCPCB fab; thicker FR4 / alt material is an option if more inner-layer margin is
# wanted. EE MUST verify 2 mm-coated meets the applicable standard before energizing.
(version 1)

(rule "HV surface creepage"
	(constraint creepage (min 2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return'"))

(rule "HV air clearance"
	(constraint clearance (min 2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return'"))

# The GND guard pour must keep the full 4 mm from HV (it is a large coplanar plane —
# creepage, not the relaxed 2 mm air figure, governs it). This makes the pour the
# 4 mm moat around every HV net while still allowing HV components 2 mm air + slots.
(rule "HV to GND pour"
	(constraint clearance (min 4mm))
	(condition "(A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return') && B.Type == 'Zone'"))

# Vertical: nothing on an adjacent layer should sit under HV copper with the
# thin 0.1 mm prepreg between F.Cu and In1. Hold inter-layer (physical) spacing
# so HV on an outer layer can't face copper directly across the 0.1 mm gap.
(rule "HV interlayer hole/pad spacing"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 1mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV_5kV' || A.NetClass == 'HV_Return'"))
